Recommend: client sends an `Idempotency-Key` header, stored as a unique `(account_id, idempotency_key)` pair on `orders`, enforced with a DB constraint rather than a check-then-insert — a check-then-insert has a race under concurrent retries (two identical requests both pass the check before either commits); a unique constraint plus `ON CONFLICT` is atomic and fits `db.write()`'s existing transaction.

